// ---------------- Stories, part ten: the 86s, 1959 to 1993 ----------------
// Same shape as before: ST(id, logline, tagline, 'setting/tod/who/caption|...', 'trailer line|...'). Cast letters only
// where the catalogue has that actor in that slot. Trailer lines name characters, never the real people who made them.
ST('waltzbashir', "An Israeli filmmaker realises he remembers nothing of his time as a young soldier in the 1982 Lebanon war, and interviews old comrades until the memory of a massacre comes back.", "The memory he lost is the one he needs.", "street/n//twenty-six snarling dogs run through a city at night|beach/n//three young soldiers float in the sea under yellow flares|city/d//a soldier dances through gunfire on a Beirut street|apartment/d//an old friend in Holland talks about the war over a joint|city/d//the animation ends; real footage of women wailing in the camp", "Twenty-six dogs.|One recurring dream.|A memory he buried.|Now he has to dig it up.");
ST('firesplain', "In the last months of the war in the Philippines, a tubercular Japanese private is thrown out by his unit and wanders the island as the army around him collapses into starvation and cannibalism.", "The war was lost. The men went on.", "jungle/d//a sick soldier is slapped and sent away by his squad leader|jungle/d//he walks through burning fields toward a column of smoke|village/n//a church in an abandoned village; a woman screams|field/d//a line of men crawls across a road under fire|jungle/d//a man walks toward the smoke of farmers' fires with his hands raised", "The army's gone.|He has a cough and six potatoes.|The men he meets are hungry.|Very hungry.");
ST('spartacus', "A Thracian slave trained as a gladiator leads a revolt that swells into an army and marches on Rome, while two senators play politics with his fate.", "The rebel who defied an empire.", "ring/d/A/a gladiator trains in the school at Capua|ring/d/A/a fight to the death for a Roman senator's amusement|mountains/d/A/the slave army camps under the stars|palace/n/B/a general tells his slave about snails and oysters|battlefield/d/A/'I'm Spartacus!' One by one, the prisoners stand", "He was a slave.|He became an army.|Rome sent its legions.|I'm Spartacus!");
ST('virginspring', "In medieval Sweden, a farmer's daughter is raped and murdered by herdsmen on her way to church, and that night the killers ask for shelter at her father's farm.", "A father's vengeance. A spring of mercy.", "farm/d//a jealous foster sister calls on Odin over the fire|forest/d//a girl in a fine dress rides through the woods to church|forest/d//herdsmen stop her by a stream|farm/n/A/a father wrestles a birch tree down, then takes his knife|forest/d/A/where her body lay, a spring rises from the earth", "A girl rides to church.|She never arrives.|Her killers knock on her father's door.|He builds a church with his own hands.");
ST('eyeswithoutface', "A brilliant surgeon kidnaps young women and removes their faces, trying to graft a new one onto his daughter, who was disfigured in a car crash he caused.", "She wears a mask so you won't see what he did.", "car/n//a woman drags a body in a raincoat to the river|mansion/n//a girl in a smooth white mask drifts through the house|hospital/n//a surgeon draws the line of the scalpel on a sleeping face|mansion/n//the dogs in the kennels howl|forest/n//a girl in a mask walks into the woods with the doves", "Her father is a great surgeon.|She has no face.|He's finding her one.|Behind the mask, something worse.");
ST('marienbad', "In a vast baroque hotel, a man tells a woman they met last year and promised to run away together, and she says she doesn't remember, or maybe it never happened.", "Last year. Or perhaps never.", "hotel/n//a voice repeats itself down endless ornate corridors|hotel/d//guests in a formal garden cast shadows; the trees don't|hotel/n//a game of matches that one man always wins|hotel/n//a woman in a feathered gown in a white bedroom|hotel/n//a man and a woman walk out into the night", "Last year at Marienbad.|Do you remember?|You don't remember?|It was here. Or somewhere else.");
ST('throughglass', "On a summer holiday on a Swedish island, a young woman released from an asylum believes God will come through the wallpaper of an empty room, and her family can't hold her.", "God is a spider.", "beach/d/A/four people come out of the sea laughing|apartment/n/A/a young woman reads her father's diary|apartment/d/A/she listens to voices behind the wallpaper|ship/d/A/a wrecked boat in a rainstorm, her brother beside her|apartment/d/A/a helicopter lands; she says she saw God, and he was a spider", "A summer on an island.|A family that can't see her.|A door in the wallpaper.|And what came through it.");
ST('aimlessbullet', "In war-ruined Seoul, an accountant with a bad tooth supports his family on almost nothing, while his mother keeps crying 'Let's go!' and his brother plans a bank robbery.", "Let's go. Where?", "apartment/n//an old woman cries 'Let's get out of here!' in the dark|office/d//a clerk works with a throbbing tooth he can't afford to fix|street/d//a younger brother, a war veteran, looks for work|street/d//a robbery and a chase through the alleys|car/n//a man in a taxi can't decide where to go", "Seoul after the war.|An honest clerk.|A brother with a gun.|A tooth that won't stop aching.");
ST('knifewater', "A smug sportswriter and his young wife pick up a hitchhiking student and take him on their yacht for the weekend, where the two men compete with a knife between them.", "Two men, one woman and one knife.", "car/d//a car nearly hits a hitchhiker on a country road|ship/d//a yacht on a Polish lake|ship/d//a knife game on the deck, fingers spread|ship/d//a struggle; the student goes over the side|car/d//the couple stop at a crossroads, not sure what to say", "One weekend.|One yacht.|One knife.|Somebody's going overboard.");
ST('sanjuro', "A scruffy, sardonic masterless samurai takes charge of nine earnest young clansmen trying to root out corruption, and keeps saving them from their own nobility.", "Nine young samurai. One who knows what he's doing.", "church/n/A/nine young men plot in a shrine; a scruffy samurai yawns in the corner|mansion/d//a gracious lady scolds him for carrying a naked sword|mansion/d//camellias float down a stream as a signal|mansion/n/A/he cuts down a row of guards in seconds|field/d/B/a duel: two men stand perfectly still, then one draws", "Nine young samurai.|One scruffy man.|White camellias. Or red.|The draw is one second long.");
ST('sahibbibi', "In decaying Calcutta aristocracy, a village servant becomes the confidant of the young wife of a debauched landlord, who drinks to win her husband back.", "A house falling to pieces, and the woman inside it.", "mansion/d//a man picks through the ruins of a great mansion|mansion/n/C/a lonely wife sends for the servant|mansion/n/C/she drinks to keep her husband home|street/d/A/a servant works in a sindoor factory|mansion/n/C/a wife's palanquin stopped in the night", "A great house.|A lonely wife.|A servant who keeps her secret.|And the bottle that keeps her husband home.");
ST('birds', "A San Francisco socialite follows a lawyer to the coastal town of Bodega Bay with a pair of lovebirds, and the birds of the town start to attack.", "The birds is coming.", "street/d//a woman buys lovebirds in a city pet shop|ship/d//a gull swoops and cuts her head as she crosses the bay|school/d//crows gather on the climbing frame behind her|school/d//schoolchildren run as the crows attack|car/u//a car edges out through a landscape of waiting birds", "It starts with a gull.|Then the crows on the schoolyard.|Then the sky.|The birds is coming.");
ST('silence63', "Two sisters and a little boy stop in a strange Central European city on the brink of war where nobody speaks their language, and one sister is dying.", "Two sisters. One city. No common language.", "train/n/A/two sisters and a boy on a train through the night|hotel/d/A/a dying translator in a grand hotel room|street/d//tanks rumble through the narrow streets|hotel/d//a boy wanders the corridors and meets a troupe of dwarves|train/d//the boy reads the words his aunt left him", "Two sisters.|A city on the edge of war.|A boy alone in the corridors.|And a few words.");
ST('servant', "A rich, idle young Londoner hires a manservant who slowly takes control of his house, his habits and finally his will.", "Who's master here?", "apartment/d/A/a manservant interviews for a job in an empty Chelsea house|apartment/d/A/he repaints, refurnishes, takes over|apartment/n//a maid seduces the master in the kitchen|apartment/n/A/master and servant play ball on the stairs|apartment/n/A/a sordid party; the fiancée leaves; the servant shuts the door", "A master.|A servant.|A house in Chelsea.|Who's master now?");
ST('hardday', "A day and a half in the life of the biggest band in the world: a train, a TV studio, a grandfather who causes trouble and a lot of running from screaming fans.", "Yeah! Yeah! Yeah!", "street/d//four young men run from screaming fans|train/d//a band plays cards in the guard's van|field/d//they jump and fool around in a field|stage/n//the TV show; the girls scream through every song|street/d//a drummer goes off to be alone and gets arrested", "Four lads.|One day and a bit.|A grandfather who's very clean.|Run!");
ST('kwaidan', "Four Japanese ghost stories: a samurai's abandoned wife, a woman of the snow, a blind musician who sings for the dead and a face in a teacup.", "Four tales of the dead.", "mansion/d//a samurai returns to the wife he abandoned|snow/n/A/a woman of snow breathes on a woodcutter|church/n//a blind musician covered in sacred writing sings for ghosts|ship/d//a painted sea battle on a golden sky|apartment/d//a man sees a face in his teacup", "Four tales.|A wife.|A woman of the snow.|A face in a cup.");
ST('reddesert', "In the poisoned industrial landscape around Ravenna, a factory engineer's wife, still shaken after a car accident, drifts through her life and an affair.", "The world is grey. She sees red.", "field/d//a woman walks through grey industrial wasteland with her son|lab/d//a factory; yellow smoke and screaming steam|bar/n//friends in a red shack by the water|bedroom/d//a hotel room; she cannot be comforted|beach/d//a girl on a pink beach, a story told to a sick boy", "Ravenna.|The factory.|The smoke.|She can't stop shaking.");
ST('hamlet64', "The prince of Denmark returns to a castle ruled by his uncle, who murdered his father and married his mother, and begins to play mad.", "To be, or not to be.", "castle/d/A/a prince arrives at the castle gates|castle/n//his father's ghost on the battlements|castle/d/A/he speaks the soliloquy by the sea|theatre/n//the players perform; the king stands up|castle/d/A/a duel with a poisoned blade", "Something is rotten in the state of Denmark.|A father's ghost on the battlements.|A play to catch a king.|The rest is silence.");
ST('blackgod', "In the drought-blasted Brazilian backlands, a cowherd who kills his boss becomes a disciple of a violent black prophet, then of a white bandit, while a hired gunman hunts them both.", "The backlands will become the sea.", "desert/d//a cowherd kneels by a dead cow in the scorched earth|desert/d//a preacher leads pilgrims up a mountain|church/d//the prophet's followers sacrifice a child|desert/d//a hired gunman spins as he shoots|beach/d//a man runs, and the backlands turn to sea", "The backlands.|A black god.|A white devil.|And the sea.");
ST('gertrud', "A former opera singer married to a lawyer leaves him for a young composer, then finds every man in her life puts something else before love.", "Love is everything.", "apartment/d//a woman tells her husband she's leaving|bedroom/n//a young composer at the piano|ballroom/n//a reception where a poet is honoured|apartment/d//she discovers the composer boasted of her|apartment/d//forty years later, she sees an old friend", "She left her husband.|She left her lover.|She left the poet.|Love was everything. They never understood.");
ST('spycold', "A burned-out British agent pretends to defect to East Germany to trap a senior Stasi officer, and finds he's only a pawn in a bigger game.", "No one leaves the cold.", "bridge/n/A/a border crossing in Berlin; a man runs and is shot|bar/n/A/an agent drinks himself into disgrace|street/d//he's recruited by the East|courtroom/d/A/a secret tribunal in East Germany|bridge/n/A/he climbs the Berlin Wall", "An agent comes in from the cold.|Or pretends to.|A secret tribunal in the East.|A wall, a searchlight, a choice.");
ST('repulsion', "A shy young manicurist left alone in her sister's South Kensington flat for a weekend loses her mind, as the walls crack and the rabbit on the plate rots.", "A woman alone in a room.", "street/d/A/a young woman walks to work in a daze|apartment/n/A/she lies awake as her sister and lover make love next door|kitchen/d/A/a rabbit rots on a plate|apartment/n/A/hands come out of the walls of the corridor|apartment/d//a family photograph; the girl's eye", "A young woman.|A flat.|A weekend.|And the walls are cracking.");
ST('redbeard', "A young doctor fresh from training in Nagasaki is sent against his will to a run-down public clinic, and its gruff, kind head teaches him what medicine is.", "Red Beard.", "hospital/d/A/a stern doctor with a red beard|hospital/d//a young doctor sulks in his fine clothes|hospital/n//a dying man tells his story|street/d/A/Red Beard fights off a gang of thugs|hospital/d//a girl the young doctor rescued nurses him", "A young doctor who wanted a court post.|A clinic for the poor.|A teacher with a red beard and fists to match.|He learns what medicine is for.");
ST('fewdollars', "Two bounty hunters, a laconic young drifter and an older colonel with a secret, team up to catch a crazed bandit with a musical pocket watch.", "The man with no name is back.", "desert/d/A/a bounty hunter rides into a dusty town|saloon/n//a colonel strikes a match on a hunchback's back|desert/d//two men shoot each other's hats off|church/n//a bandit high on a joint|desert/d/A/a pocket watch chimes; the duel", "Two bounty hunters.|One bandit.|A pocket watch that chimes before every killing.|When the chimes finish, pick up your gun.");
ST('guide65', "A tour guide falls for a dancer trapped in a loveless marriage to an archaeologist, ruins her, goes to prison for forgery, and later is taken for a holy man by a drought-stricken village.", "A guide who was taken for a saint.", "desert/d/AB/a guide shows a dancer the caves near Udaipur|stage/n/B/a dancer finds fame with the snake dance|prison/d/A/he's jailed for forging her signature|village/d/A/villagers think he's a holy man|village/d/A/a man fasts for rain until it comes", "A guide.|A dancer.|A forger.|A saint.");
ST('tokyoolympiad', "The 1964 Tokyo Olympics, seen not as results but as athletes' bodies, faces, sweat and nerves, and the crowds who came to watch them.", "Tokyo, 1964.", "street/d//a wrecking ball swings; a city rebuilds itself|field/d//the torch is carried up Mount Fuji|ring/d//sprinters in the blocks, their faces close-up|field/d//a long-distance runner alone on the road|field/n//the closing ceremony, the athletes mingling", "A city rebuilds itself.|A torch climbs a mountain.|A runner alone on the road.|Not who won. What it felt like.");
ST('manforallseasons', "Thomas More, England's Lord Chancellor, refuses to approve Henry VIII's divorce and his break with Rome, and quietly, cleverly, keeps his silence all the way to the block.", "A man for all seasons.", "palace/d/B/a dying cardinal in red tells him to sign|mansion/d//the king leaps off his barge into the mud of More's garden|courtroom/d/A/he's tried for treason; the perjured witness is rewarded with Wales|prison/d/A/his family visits him in the Tower|street/d/A/he forgives the executioner and puts his head on the block", "The king wants a divorce.|The Chancellor won't sign.|Silence is not a crime.|Yet.");
ST('blowup', "A fashionable London photographer secretly snaps a couple in a park, and when he blows up the pictures he thinks he's photographed a murder.", "Murder or mime?", "street/d//a van of mime artists in white face pass through the city|apartment/d//a photographer straddles a model on the floor|forest/d//a couple embraces in a park|lab/n//he blows up the photographs, and finds a body in the bushes|ring/d//mimes play tennis with an imaginary ball", "A photographer.|A couple in a park.|Blow it up. Then blow it up again.|Is that a body in the bushes?");
ST('daisies', "Two teenage girls named Marie decide that since the world is spoiled, they'll be spoiled too, and pull a series of pranks on rich men and a banquet.", "Two girls, one world, all spoiled.", "field/d//two girls in bikinis sit like dolls|bar/n//they cheat a sugar daddy out of dinner|apartment/d//they cut each other up with scissors|ballroom/d//they eat and destroy a banquet|ballroom/d//a chandelier falls", "Two Maries.|The world's spoiled.|So they'll be spoiled too.|Pass the cake.");
ST('seconds', "A middle-aged banker is given a new face, a new identity and a new life as a painter in Malibu by a secret company, and finds he can't live it.", "A second chance at life.", "train/d//a man on a train is handed a slip of paper|office/d//a company offers him a second life|hospital/d//he wakes up with a new face|ballroom/n/A/a wine party; a man goes to pieces|hospital/d/A/the company comes for him", "A banker buys a second life.|A new face. A studio in Malibu.|He can't stop being himself.|The company has a policy on returns.");
ST('nayak', "A matinee idol on a train from Calcutta to Delhi gives an interview to a young journalist and slowly reveals the doubts, failures and nightmares under his glamour.", "The hero.", "train/d/A/a film star boards a train|train/d/B/a journalist sets out to interview him|bedroom/n/A/a nightmare: he's sinking in banknotes|stage/d/A/a flashback: his old theatre teacher|train/d/B/she tears up her notes", "The biggest star in Bengal.|One train journey.|A journalist who asks the wrong questions.|In his dream, the money is drowning him.");
ST('nightlivingdead', "On a Pennsylvania night, a brother and sister are attacked in a cemetery and a group of strangers barricade themselves in a farmhouse as the dead rise.", "They're coming to get you, Barbara.", "church/d//a brother and sister visit a grave; a stranger staggers toward them|farm/n//strangers board up the farmhouse windows|farm/n//the radio reports the dead are coming back|farm/n//a girl in the cellar picks up a trowel|field/d//a man at the window at dawn; the posse arrives", "They're coming to get you, Barbara.|A farmhouse.|Seven strangers.|The dead don't stay dead.");
ST('ifdotdot', "At an English public school, a rebellious senior and his friends suffer prefects, canings and chapel, and then take up arms on Founder's Day.", "Which side will you be on?", "school/d/A/a rebellious boy returns to school with a moustache|school/d//prefects cane the boys in the gym|bar/d/A/a girl in a café; they wrestle like tigers|school/d/A/they find guns in the crypt|school/d/A/Founder's Day: the boys open fire from the roof", "Which side will you be on?|Prefects. Canings. Chapel.|A cache of guns in the crypt.|Founder's Day.");
ST('butchcassidy', "Two charming outlaws find the Wild West closing in on them, and when a relentless posse won't quit, they run to Bolivia.", "Not that it matters, but most of it is true.", "train/d/A/a train robbery; the safe blows up|field/d/A/a bicycle ride with a girl and a song|mountains/d/A/a posse that won't quit: 'Who are those guys?'|mountains/d/AB/they jump off a cliff into a river|village/d/AB/two men run out into a hail of bullets; the frame freezes", "Who are those guys?|A cliff and a river.|A bicycle and a song.|Bolivia.");
ST('zmovie', "A leftist deputy is killed in a staged traffic accident in an unnamed Mediterranean country, and an investigating magistrate refuses to accept the cover-up.", "He is alive.", "street/d/A/a deputy speaks at a rally|street/n//a man is struck on the head by a truck|office/d/B/a young magistrate investigates|office/d/B/the generals are charged|street/d//the coup; Z is banned", "A deputy speaks for peace.|A truck in the night.|A magistrate who won't let it go.|He is alive.");
ST('thecow', "In a poor Iranian village, a man's beloved cow dies while he's away, and the villagers tell him she ran off, until he starts to believe he is the cow.", "He loved his cow.", "village/d/A/a man washes his cow in the pond|village/d//villagers bury the cow while he's away|village/d/A/they tell him she ran away|farm/n/A/he moves into the cow shed and eats hay|village/d//the villagers drag him to town on a rope", "A man loves his cow.|The cow dies.|The village says she ran away.|So he becomes her.");
ST('mash', "At a mobile army surgical hospital in the Korean war, two irreverent surgeons fight the war with jokes, martinis and pranks on the camp's prigs.", "M*A*S*H.", "hospital/d//helicopters land with the wounded|hospital/d/A/two surgeons operate under fire|field/n//a tent; the officers' sex life is on the loudspeaker|field/d//a football game, rigged|hospital/d/A/a dentist's 'suicide', with the Last Supper", "Korea.|Two surgeons with no respect for rank.|A rigged football game.|Suicide is painless.");
ST('patton', "An American general in the Second World War, brilliant, vain and impossible, wins in Africa and Sicily, slaps a soldier, and is sidelined until the Bulge.", "Patton.", "stage/d/A/a general addresses the troops in front of a giant flag|desert/d/A/a tank battle in North Africa|hospital/d/A/he slaps a soldier with shell shock|snow/d/A/he leads the army through the snow|field/d/A/a general walks his dog in the windmill fields", "Old blood and guts.|Africa. Sicily. The Bulge.|He slapped a soldier and lost a command.|He wanted the war to go on forever.");
ST('fiveeasypieces', "A former piano prodigy working on an oil rig goes home to his family of musicians when his father has a stroke, bringing his waitress girlfriend.", "He rode the fast lane on the road to nowhere.", "field/d/A/a man works on an oil rig|car/d/A/a traffic jam; he plays piano on the back of a truck|diner/d/A/the chicken salad sandwich, hold the chicken|mansion/d/A/a family of musicians on an island|diner/d/A/a petrol station; he hitches a ride on a truck going north", "He was a piano prodigy.|Now he works an oil field.|A chicken salad sandwich, hold the chicken.|A truck heading north.");
ST('daysnightsforest', "Four young Calcutta men drive to the forests of Palamau for a holiday, bribe their way into a forest bungalow, and the women they meet show them how shallow they are.", "Days and nights in the forest.", "car/d//four friends drive out of Calcutta|forest/d//they bribe the caretaker for a bungalow|forest/d/AB/a memory game on a picnic: famous names|forest/n//a fair; a tribal woman|forest/d/B/a man and a woman in the trees", "Four city friends.|A forest bungalow.|A memory game.|The women were always smarter.");
ST('wakeinfright', "A schoolteacher on his way to Sydney for Christmas gets stranded in an outback mining town, where the hospitality is drink and more drink, and a kangaroo hunt.", "Have a drink, mate.", "desert/d//a train in the desert; a schoolteacher leaves the outback|bar/n//he's stranded in a mining town; they buy him beer|bar/n//a two-up game; he loses everything|desert/n//a kangaroo hunt in the night|desert/d//he tries to leave", "Have a drink, mate.|Have another.|A two-up game you can't win.|There's no getting out of the Yabba.");
ST('emigrants', "In the 1840s, a poor Swedish farming family and their neighbours give up their stony land and emigrate to America, surviving the voyage and the long trek to Minnesota.", "The emigrants.", "farm/d/A/a farmer breaks his back on stony Swedish fields|apartment/d/B/a little girl dies after eating the barley porridge|ship/d/B/ten weeks in the hold of a sailing ship, lice and fever|ship/n//a woman dies at sea; the body is lowered over the side|forest/d/A/they reach a lake in Minnesota and he marks out the land", "A stony farm in Sweden.|A family that's had enough.|Ten weeks at sea.|America, at any price.");
ST('loving71', "A dying old woman in 1950s Budapest is told her son is a film director in America, when he's actually in prison, and his wife writes the letters.", "Love.", "bedroom/d//an old woman in bed, being lied to|apartment/d//a daughter-in-law writes letters from America|prison/d//a man in a prison|street/d//the old woman's memories of the past|apartment/d//the son comes home", "An old woman is dying.|Her son is in prison.|His wife writes his letters from America.|A lie told out of love.");
ST('moncleantoine', "On Christmas Eve in an asbestos-mining town in Quebec, a teenage boy helps his uncle, the undertaker, fetch a body from a farm through the snow.", "My uncle Antoine.", "village/d//the asbestos mines in winter|village/d//a general store on Christmas Eve|snow/n//a boy and his uncle drive a sleigh through the snow|snow/n//the coffin falls off the sleigh|farm/n//a boy looks through a window at a grieving family", "Christmas Eve in a mining town.|An uncle who sells everything, coffins included.|A sleigh ride through the snow.|A boy learns what grown-ups are.");
ST('americangraffiti', "On the last night of summer 1962 in a California town, a gang of friends cruise the strip and look for a blonde in a white Thunderbird before two of them leave for college.", "Where were you in '62?", "diner/n/A/a drive-in diner; carhops on roller skates|car/n/A/he chases a blonde in a white Thunderbird|car/n/C/a drag race at dawn|car/n/B/a couple fight in the car|ship/d/A/a plane takes off; he looks down at the white car", "Where were you in '62?|One last night of summer.|A blonde in a white Thunderbird.|Cruise the strip till dawn.");
ST('meanstreets', "In Little Italy, a small-time hood with a conscience tries to rise in his uncle's world while protecting his reckless friend, who owes everyone money.", "You don't make up for your sins in church.", "church/n/A/a man holds his finger over a church candle|bar/n/A/a red-lit bar; 'Jumpin' Jack Flash'|street/n/B/a reckless friend blows up a mailbox|bar/n//a pool hall fight|car/n/AB/a car is shot at; blood on the window", "You don't make up for your sins in church.|You do it on the streets.|A friend who owes everybody.|Jumpin' Jack Flash.");
ST('motherwhore', "A young Parisian idler living with his older girlfriend starts an affair with a nurse, and the three talk, drink and torture each other in the wake of May '68.", "The mother and the whore.", "bar/d/A/a young man in a café|apartment/d/A/he lives with an older woman|hospital/d//a nurse he picks up in the street|apartment/n//three people in bed, talking|apartment/n//a long monologue on sex and love", "A young man who talks.|A woman who keeps him.|A nurse who sleeps with everyone.|Three and a half hours of the truth.");
ST('youngfrankenstein', "Dr. Frederick Frankenstein ('That's Fronkensteen') inherits his grandfather's castle in Transylvania and decides to continue his experiments.", "The scariest comedy of all time.", "lab/d/A/a lecture; 'That's Fronkensteen!'|train/d/A/the train to Transylvania|castle/n/A/a hunchback named Igor ('That's Eye-gor')|lab/n/A/the creature comes alive|stage/n/A/'Puttin' on the Ritz'", "That's Fronkensteen.|That's Eye-gor.|Frau Blücher! (horses whinny)|Puttin' on the Ritz.");
ST('sholay', "A retired police chief hires two small-time crooks to capture the dacoit Gabbar Singh, who murdered his family and took his arms.", "The flames of revenge.", "train/d/AB/two crooks fight off bandits on a train|village/d/C/a retired cop hires them|village/d//Gabbar Singh's lair: 'How many men were there?'|mountains/d/B/a motorbike with a sidecar; 'Yeh Dosti'|village/d/C/the cop's arms were cut off", "Two crooks.|One retired cop with no arms.|One bandit the hills fear.|How many men were there?");
ST('dersuuzala', "A Russian army surveyor mapping the Siberian wilderness befriends a Goldi hunter, who saves his life in the forest and then can't survive the city.", "A friend of the forest.", "forest/d//a surveying party in the Siberian wilderness|forest/n//a hunter by the campfire|snow/d//a blizzard on a frozen lake; the hunter builds a shelter|apartment/d//the hunter in the city|forest/d//a grave in the forest", "A surveyor maps the taiga.|A hunter who reads the forest.|A blizzard on a frozen lake.|The city has no room for him.");
ST('manwhowouldbeking', "Two former British soldiers in India set out for remote Kafiristan to become kings, and one of them is taken for a god.", "Adventure in the remote lands of Kafiristan.", "office/n//a journalist in India meets two adventurers|mountains/d/AB/they climb the Himalayas|battlefield/d/A/a battle; an arrow in his chest|palace/d/A/he's worshipped as a god|bridge/d/A/a rope bridge over a chasm", "Two old soldiers.|One contract.|A kingdom past the edge of the map.|A god doesn't bleed. Does he?");
ST('criacuervos', "After her father dies, a solemn eight-year-old girl in a Madrid house believes she has the power to kill, and her dead mother keeps coming back.", "Raise ravens.", "mansion/n/B/a girl finds her father dead in bed|mansion/d/A/her dead mother visits her|mansion/d/B/she poisons her aunt's milk, or thinks she does|mansion/d//the girls dance to 'Porque te vas'|school/d//a school day", "Raise ravens and they'll peck out your eyes.|A girl who thinks she can kill.|A dead mother who visits.|Why are you leaving?");
