ST('elephantman', "In Victorian London, a surgeon rescues a severely deformed man from a freak show and discovers a gentle, cultured soul inside, while society queues up to stare.", "I am not an animal!", "street/n/B/a surgeon pays a penny to see the freak behind a curtain|hospital/d/A/the man recites the 23rd Psalm, past the lines he was taught|apartment/d/A/he builds a model of the cathedral he can see from his window|street/n/A/cornered by a mob in a station: 'I am not an animal! I am a human being!'|bedroom/n/A/he takes the pillows away and lies down to sleep like everyone else", "A freak show.|A surgeon.|A man nobody looked in the eye.|I am not an animal!");
