ST('babettesfeast', "In a remote Danish village, a French refugee cook spends her lottery winnings on one magnificent dinner for her two pious employers and their dwindling congregation.", "Babette's feast.", "village/d//two pious sisters on the windswept coast of Jutland|kitchen/d/A/a French cook arrives in the rain with a letter of introduction|ship/d/A/a boat brings live quail, a turtle and crates of wine|ballroom/n//the congregation swear not to taste the food; a general can't stop talking about it|kitchen/n/A/she says she spent all her money on the dinner", "Two sisters.|A cook.|Ten thousand francs.|One dinner.");
